# Line endings.
#
# Every text file is stored and checked out as LF, on every platform. Without
# `eol=lf`, a Windows clone with `core.autocrlf=true` gets CRLF on disk while the
# repository holds LF — and `pnpm format:check` then fails on *every* file,
# because Prettier's `endOfLine` default is `lf`. That is how the 122-file
# figure in Sprint 1 task 1 was measured: only 74 of those files had a real
# formatting problem, the rest were line endings.
#
# `text=auto` still lets git detect binary content, so the rule is safe to apply
# with `*`; the explicit entries below are belt and braces.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
